7. TEST FINDER GOTCHA WORTH REMEMBERING
---------------------------------------
The old order card and tab-bar widgets shared the words "New" and "Approved",
so `find.text('New')` was ambiguous. Those two widgets (`OrderTabs`,
`OrderCard`) have since been deleted; the Orders screen now renders a stream of
history rows and its test scopes finders by ancestor rather than by those types.

The general lesson still holds: when two UI regions legitimately show the same
word, scope the finder (by ancestor/descendant) instead of asserting on bare
`find.text`, and never leave a bare `find.text('New')` in the orders tests.


